**Issue:** A commit after every single insert.
**Why:** Each commit forces an fsync; per-row commits turn a bulk load into thousands of durable transactions (an N+1 on transaction boundaries).
**Fix:**
def save_all(items):
    try:
        for it in items:
            db.execute('INSERT INTO items (name) VALUES (%s)', (it.name,))
        db.commit()
    except Exception:
        db.rollback()
        raise

