**Issue:** One permissions query per user in the serialization loop.
**Why:** An API returning 100 users fires 101 queries; permissions are also shared roles, so results repeat.
**Fix:**
def permissions_for(users):
    rows = db.execute('SELECT user_id, perm FROM perms WHERE user_id = ANY(%s)',
                      ([u.id for u in users],)).fetchall()
    table = {}
    for uid, perm in rows:
        table.setdefault(uid, set()).add(perm)
    return {u.id: table.get(u.id, set()) for u in users}

